  "id": "t13-fanout-clamp-not-an-integer-warning",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), representative of items 10-11 of the versioned inventory (contract assertion 24, LOHRA_MAX_PARALLEL clamp table): LOHRA_MAX_PARALLEL='abc' (non-numeric) falls back to the default (4) and emits a byte-exact stderr warning naming the offending value via Python's own repr() convention. This is exactly the observable a unit test cannot prove: the candidate's own clamp-table unit tests (tests/orchestration-fanout-config.test.ts) already verify the CANDIDATE's warning matches what its own code believes the oracle says — only the wire proves it is what the oracle actually says. No spawn needed at all: the warning fires unconditionally during startup, before any tool call, so this is the simplest possible manifest (a single parent round trip, no orchestration surface touched).",
